   "html_text": "Foot begins her investigation of the connection between virtue and the will by examining the role of intention in the assessment of character. In her view, we evaluate a person’s moral quality primarily through their intentions (1978 [VV 4]). Yet good intentions alone are not sufficient to establish that someone possesses virtue. In the case of charity or benevolence, a person may reveal a lack of charity despite having good intentions if they fail to bring about the intended good. One may, for ",
